# Updated by Alice 2/5/2025 - key files added and comments on why! especially .env - learning takeaway - always add API keys in a .env file and never track .env files or .env.local files
# ^ As this poses a security risk, see below why
# Python -
#  the below 2 were added to gitignore since .pyc files are python compiled files that are encoded in bytecode form for faster re-use
# ^ and live in __pycache__/ folders - they are auto-generated, machine-dependent, not human readable, and they change every time you run code, so there is
# ^ no point tracking them in git! :)
*.pyc
__pycache__/

# Node/React Frontend:
node_modules/
.next/
.env.local
*.log
node_modules/package-lock.json
package-lock.json

# macOS system junk
.DS_Store

# Python backend
venv/

# Django stuff
upf_backend/db.sqlite3
upf_backend/chatbot/.env

# General env files - .env was not added before which poses a security risk - bots will scan through github for .env files 
# Best practice in group projects: EACH DEVELOPER SHOULD USE THEIR OWN API KEY ESPECIALLY if there are usage limits, quotas, or billing risks
.env 
.env.local